# While spork 19 is off, a block above the held lock takes the active chain onto a fork the lock
# conflicts with below its height. The block is no conflict itself, but the reorg connects the
# fork's blocks unmarked (validation.cpp:2527, gated by chainlock/chainlock.cpp:73-82). Back on,
# the timer's enforcement walks back to the lock.
extend main 3
fork 2 2
cl main@-0
spork off
extend b1 1
spork on
extend main 1
